# Sync-tool duplicates: "Dockerfile 2", "package 2.json", "index 2.html".
# A file-sync path drops byte-identical copies next to the originals — 13 of
# them are sitting in this working tree right now, untracked but unignored, so
# one `git add -A` commits the lot. A duplicate Dockerfile or deploy.sh is a
# live trap for whoever edits the wrong one.
#
# Deliberately not a blanket "* [0-9].*": that would silently swallow a
# legitimately named "Phase 2.md", and an ignored file you meant to commit is
# the worse failure. Only the types where a stray copy does damage.
* [0-9].py
* [0-9].ts
* [0-9].tsx
* [0-9].js
* [0-9].jsx
* [0-9].json
* [0-9].yml
* [0-9].yaml
* [0-9].sh
* [0-9].html
* [0-9].sql
* [0-9].toml
Dockerfile [0-9]
